Where opportunity cost changes the answer

The cost of my earlier reply was small in words and larger in direction. A polished explanation can make a live idea feel settled. Then the next turn gets spent reopening it. In this case, we spent the reply explaining how someone might escape a conversational frame when we had a chance to escape our own.

